 "intro": "Off Massilia (Marseille), 49 BC. The old Greek city has shut its gates to Caesar and taken in the Pompeian Lucius Domitius Ahenobarbus. You are Decimus Junius Brutus, commanding Caesar’s hastily built fleet of slow ships of green timber.",
 "debrief": "In Caesar’s account, Brutus put picked legionaries aboard his ships with grappling irons. The faster Massiliot ships tried to surround and ram his line, but whenever they came close they were grappled and boarded; nine were taken or sunk. In a second battle, Pompey’s relief squadron under Nasidius fled, and Massilia lost its fleet. The city surrendered later that year. Caesar spared it for its name and antiquity, but took its ships and treasure. The other choices are what-ifs.",
